<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.3.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00099</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.3.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>d749fea7-ffc9-4229-afef-82bbae1cdef8</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">For questions 1 - 2, use the following scenario to identify the equation described.</para>
      <para id="para-00003"><quote id="quote-00001">Two different telephone carriers offer the following plans that a person is considering. Company A has a monthly fee of $20 and charges $0.05/minute for calls. Company B has a monthly fee of $5 and charges $0.10/minute for calls.</quote></para>
      <exercise id="_7d1d5fe2-34d3-4b58-b950-b8f1569aaf7c" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">Find the model for the entire  cost, c,  when Company A’s plan is used for m minutes.</para>
          <para id="para-00005">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>0.05</m:mn><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>0.10</m:mn><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>0.10</m:mn><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>0.05</m:mn><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00010">Try again. Revisit activity 1.3.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00011">The correct answer is c=20 + 0.05m.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="fdcc69e8-e6b8-4757-8482-f965eaf43aea" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00012">Find the model for the entire cost, c, when  Company B’s plan is used for m minutes.</para>
          <para id="para-00013">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>0.05</m:mn><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>0.10</m:mn><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>0.10</m:mn><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>0.05</m:mn><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00018">Try again. Revisit activity 1.3.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00019">The correct answer is b. c= 5 + 0.10m.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="b9826d19-a329-447c-b724-3006ce30ff6d" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00020">If a carpenter sawed a 10-ft board into two sections and one section was n ft long, how long would the other section, S, be in terms of n ?</para>
          <para id="para-00021">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>S</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>S</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>S</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>S</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00026">Try again. Revisit activity 1.3.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00027">The correct answer is S=10-n.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <para id="para-00028">Use the table below for problems 4 and 5:</para>
      <para id="para-00029"><quote id="quote-00002">Tyler needs to complete this table for his consumer science class. He knows that 1 tablespoon contains 3 teaspoons and that 1 cup contains 16 tablespoons.</quote></para>
      <table class="os-raise-midsizetable unnumbered" id="table-00001">
        <tgroup cols="3">
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <entry>a. ____ </entry>
              <entry>b. ____ </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00030">2</para>
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00031">36</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00032">12</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>c. ____ </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>d. ____ </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00033">48</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00034">3</para>
              </entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
      <exercise id="_02155fb4-2142-451f-b47b-3794b757c877" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00035">For each of the missing spaces in the table above, a-d, select the missing value that helps complete the table.</para>
          <para id="para-00036">a.________</para>
          <para id="para-00037">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00039">32</para>
          <para id="para-00040">64</para>
          <para id="para-00041">96</para>
          <para id="para-00042">144</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00043">Try again. Revisit activity 1.3.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00044">The correct answer is 96.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="e073cd7e-6a31-4135-ad9c-2fb461b3d392" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00045">b.________</para>
          <para id="para-00046">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00048">32</para>
          <para id="para-00049">64</para>
          <para id="para-00050">96</para>
          <para id="para-00051">144</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00052">Try again. Revisit activity 1.3.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00053">The correct answer is 32.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_01389e45-0f85-49f5-ab9c-a627dd91487e" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00054">c.________</para>
          <para id="para-00055">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00057">32</para>
          <para id="para-00058">64</para>
          <para id="para-00059">96</para>
          <para id="para-00060">144</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00061">Try again. Revisit activity 1.3.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00062">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_487b241e-1926-4620-b221-e8022719898d" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00063">d.________</para>
          <para id="para-00064">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00066">32</para>
          <para id="para-00067">64</para>
          <para id="para-00068">96</para>
          <para id="para-00069">144</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00070">Try again. Revisit activity 1.3.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00071">The correct answer is 144.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_4c5a24e4-2130-4cb9-a292-f9af235512dd" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00072">Choose the equation that represents the number of teaspoons, t, contained in a cup, C.</para>
          <para id="para-00073">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>48</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mrow><m:mn>48</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>48</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00078">Try again. Revisit activity 1.3.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00079">The correct answer is (c=\frac t{48}\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_5cc7c5b1-deb6-422d-998d-0274bdde0e79" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00009">
          <para id="para-00080">The volume of dry goods, like apples or peaches, can be measured using bushels, pecks, and quarts. A bushel contains 4 pecks, and a peck contains 8 quarts. What is the relationship between the number of bushels, b, and the number of quarts, q?</para>
          <para id="para-00081">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mi>q</m:mi><m:mrow><m:mn>32</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mi>q</m:mi><m:mrow><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mi>q</m:mi><m:mrow><m:mn>64</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>32</m:mn><m:mi>q</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">
          <para id="para-00086">Try again. Revisit activity 1.3.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00087">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mi>q</m:mi><m:mrow><m:mn>32</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>